refreshTokens

For secure login.

Instead of forcing users to log in every few minutes, we store refresh tokens separately.

The AI architecture (the exciting part)

This is where the app becomes different from every CRUD project.

The AI never talks directly to MongoDB.

Instead:

User

↓

Frontend

↓

Backend

↓

MongoDB
      │
      │
      ├── Transactions
      ├── Budgets
      └── Categories

↓

Backend summarizes data

↓

OpenAI

↓

AI Response

↓

Frontend

Example:

The user asks:

Can I afford a new laptop?

The backend will:

Fetch their transactions.
Calculate current balance.
Calculate monthly income.
Calculate monthly expenses.
Calculate savings.
Build a context object.
Send only that context plus the user's question to the AI.
Return the AI's answer.

That approach matches the PRD's requirement that the AI answer only using the user's financial data and stay within the app's scope.

Next session

We'll begin Phase 3 (Backend) by designing the database schemas before writing any endpoints.

The order will be:

User model
Transaction model
Budget model
Category model
ChatHistory model

Once those are solid, we'll build the authentication system and then the Transaction CRUD APIs. That foundation will make the frontend much easier to connect later.